From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:18:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: report DSCP Policy Query and Response frames on ubus

EasyMesh 6.1 section 20.2.4 has a Multi-AP Agent tunnel the body of each
DSCP Policy Query and DSCP Policy Response frame it receives to its
Controller. Report both as the action-frame notification, types
dscp-query and dscp-response, with the body from the Category octet, as
the BTM Query and the WNM Notification Request are reported.

The report comes before hostapd's own handling and does not depend on
the DSCP Policy capability of the station: the agent tunnels every such
frame of a BSS that advertises the capability. Unprotected frames stay
dropped.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -9867,7 +9867,7 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ROBUST_AV
 static void hostapd_dscp_action(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct sta_info *sta,
-				const u8 *pos, const u8 *end)
+				const u8 *body, const u8 *pos, const u8 *end)
 {
 	u8 subtype;
 
@@ -9882,9 +9882,13 @@
 	subtype = *pos++;
 	switch (subtype) {
 	case QM_DSCP_POLICY_QUERY:
+		hostapd_ubus_notify_action_frame(hapd, "dscp-query", sta->addr,
+						 body, end - body);
 		hostapd_handle_dscp_policy_query(hapd, sta, pos, end - pos);
 		break;
 	case QM_DSCP_POLICY_RESP:
+		hostapd_ubus_notify_action_frame(hapd, "dscp-response",
+						 sta->addr, body, end - body);
 		hostapd_handle_dscp_policy_response(hapd, sta, pos, end - pos);
 		break;
 	default:
@@ -9924,7 +9928,8 @@
 				   "DSCP: Ignoring unprotected frame");
 			return -1;
 		}
-		hostapd_dscp_action(hapd, sta, pos, end);
+		hostapd_dscp_action(hapd, sta, (const u8 *) &mgmt->u.action,
+				    pos, end);
 		return 0;
 #endif /* CONFIG_ROBUST_AV */
 	default:
